<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Sandur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1713 CE – 1949 CE (approx.) · capital Sandur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Maratha state ringed by hills in the Bellary country, ruled by the Ghorpade family and rich in iron and manganese.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sandur was taken around 1713 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddoji-rao-ghorpade">Siddoji Rao Ghorpade</a>, of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> family that had served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and his successors. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghorpade">Ghorpades</a> held the valley through the struggles between the Marathas, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled a small valley enclosed by hills in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madras-presidency">Madras Presidency</a>, with temples such as the Kumaraswamy shrine. The surrounding hills held rich deposits of iron and manganese ore. The last ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yeshwantrao-ghorpade">Yeshwantrao Ghorpade</a>, was noted for progressive administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sandur merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madras-presidency">Madras Province</a> in 1949 and passed to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mysore-state">Mysore State</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, in 1953. Mining around Sandur in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ballari">Ballari</a> district remains important.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sandur-state.jpg" alt="Sandur State" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sandur_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1713 CE – 1949 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sandur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Siddoji Rao Ghorpade, Yeshwantrao Ghorpade</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sandur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1831&amp;focus=sandur-state" aria-label="Sandur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6771 1616 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sandur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7091 1872L7364 1601M7091 1872L7364 1602M7091 1872L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7091 1872h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7091 1872h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1831&amp;focus=sandur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
